---
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/dotfiles-agents-sync-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/dotfiles-agents-sync-dark.svg?raw';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={400}
  caption="Any failed check stops the sync before the config file is touched."
>
  The Codex config sync runs five checks in order before one write. One: compare
  the shared settings with the local config and refuse a differing value. Two:
  refuse if a Codex process is running. Three: parse the new text and refuse if
  anything other than the missing settings changed. Four: re-read the file on
  disk and refuse if it changed mid-run. Five: check for a Codex process again
  and refuse if one has started. Then swap in the new file and save its digest
  in the receipt.
</Diagram>
